## 0. How to read

Four evidence categories, never merged. A green Go test is not Pekko parity.

| Code | Category | Meaning here |
|---|---|---|
| **AD** | ACCEPTED DESIGN | A decision or ADR the Owner accepted (not "Proposed"). Says nothing about code. |
| **II** | INTEGRATED IMPLEMENTATION | Code on `develop` at the audited head. Says nothing about whether it was run. |
| **RE** | RECORDED EXECUTION | A run with SHA and time written in a repo file or PR comment, with who ran it. Not re-run here. |
| **CD** | COMPARATIVELY DEMONSTRATED | Behavior shown by tests that **ran** against two engines (table A) or against Pekko (table B). Reading Pekko source is **alignment by reading**, never CD. |

Fault technique: **REAL** (real engine behavior), **SIM** (test-owned proxy, driver wrapper or injected error against a real engine), **MOCK** (`pgxmock`, `sqlitemock`, no engine). Reading labels: **(L)** read by the auditor at the cited line; **(R)** taken from a recorded run; **(X)** inference. Levels L0-L4 are those of `gopekko-testint/README.md` (L0 double, L1 real engine logic, L2 client SIGKILL, L3 engine hard stop, L4 power loss). "Not demonstrated" never means "not supported".

